{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789266430,"nonce":"mnebon/91b4IPsHUiADb0oTRYXU=","title":"Haxe objects through the protocol: index, iterate, exception message, i64","message":"Gaps in caribou-ash's HaxeRef protocol after the first crossing:\nindex/set_index/len/iterate answer Unsupported (hl.types.ArrayObj and\nArrayBytes need the element-type-aware accessors); a thrown Haxe\nexception object reports its class name as the message rather than\ncalling its message getter (no user code is run while building the\nerror); HI64 returns are widened to f64 and lose precision above 2^53.\nAlso: Wren error strings raised through the protocol are rooted by a VM\nhandle that is never released, one slot per raised error; release it\nwhen the core Error that owns it dies (a drop hook on the Error, or the\nproxy work above).","files":null}]}